    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266-a1">

                <pb facs="0695" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v20/pg667"/>


                <head>Draft Message From the Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State, at
                        London<anchor n="5" xml:id="d266-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                        1957</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>“At conference with the President he agrees generally with the statement quoted
                    below from Admiral Strauss, (quote
                        statement)<anchor n="6" xml:id="d266-f2"/></p>
                <p>“With respect to the flexibility mentioned in my former message<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d266-f3"/> the President by no means meant to convey the thought
                    that we should abandon the “inseparability concept” as between testing
                    suspension and “cut-off” of new fissionable material for weapons purposes. <pb
                        facs="0696" n="668" xml:id="pg668"/> He was more concerned that we had
                    publicly fixed ten months as the limitation of a suspension period
                        presumably<anchor n="8" xml:id="d266-f4"/> not susceptible in any way to
                        negotiations.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d266-f5"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d266-f1" n="5" type="source" xml:id="d266-f1-content">
                <p>Top Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d266-f2" n="6" xml:id="d266-f2-content">
                <p>Included in the subenclosure, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d266-f3" n="7" xml:id="d266-f3-content">
                <p>A handwritten note on the margin of the source text reads: “Herter Memorandum for the Secretary of July
                    26.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d266-f4" n="8" xml:id="d266-f4-content">
                <p>The words “suspension” and “presumably” have been handwritten on the source
                    text.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d266-f5" n="9" xml:id="d266-f5-content">
                <p>The above two sentences were transmitted in Tedul 5 to London, July 30, (Department of State, Central Files,
                    110.11–DU/7–3057) An additional sentence deleted from the source text reads:
                    “Our fundamental concepts as now understood will continue to guide our general
                    conduct in negotiations unless and until some revision has been approved by all
                    interested agencies of government.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
